@startuml Data Ingestion Flow
!theme plain

title Data Ingestion Flow Diagram

actor User
participant "Flask Dashboard\n:5000" as Dashboard
participant "Backend API\n:8000" as BackendAPI
database "SQLite DB" as DB

== CSV File Upload ==
User -> Dashboard: Upload CSV File
activate Dashboard
Dashboard -> BackendAPI: POST /new\nmultipart/form-data\nfile: CSV
activate BackendAPI

BackendAPI -> BackendAPI: Parse CSV\nRead rows
BackendAPI -> BackendAPI: For each row:\nConvert to JSON
BackendAPI -> DB: INSERT INTO csv_data\n(upload_timestamp, row_data)
activate DB
DB --> BackendAPI: Rows Inserted
deactivate DB
BackendAPI --> Dashboard: 200 OK\n{message, rows_inserted}
deactivate BackendAPI
Dashboard --> User: Success Message
deactivate Dashboard

== Data Validation ==
User -> Dashboard: Click "Validate Data"
activate Dashboard
Dashboard -> BackendAPI: PUT /validate\nHeader: X-Database-Name
activate BackendAPI

BackendAPI -> DB: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM csv_data
activate DB
DB --> BackendAPI: Total Rows
deactivate DB

BackendAPI -> BackendAPI: Calculate:\n30% = Training\n70% = Testing
BackendAPI -> BackendAPI: Randomly assign T field

BackendAPI -> DB: UPDATE csv_data\nSET T = 'training' (30%)\nSET T = 'testing' (70%)
activate DB
DB --> BackendAPI: Updated
deactivate DB

BackendAPI --> Dashboard: 200 OK\n{training_count, testing_count}
deactivate BackendAPI
Dashboard --> User: Validation Complete
deactivate Dashboard

== JSON Data Insert ==
User -> Dashboard: Enter JSON Data
activate Dashboard
Dashboard -> BackendAPI: POST /insert\n{field1: value1, ...}
activate BackendAPI

BackendAPI -> BackendAPI: Convert to JSON string
BackendAPI -> DB: INSERT INTO inserted_data\n(created_timestamp, data)
activate DB
DB --> BackendAPI: Inserted ID
deactivate DB
BackendAPI --> Dashboard: 200 OK\n{id, message}
deactivate BackendAPI
Dashboard --> User: Data Inserted
deactivate Dashboard

@enduml
